          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "# How to use this workbook\n\n**Purpose:** technical readiness review of **SQL Server enabled by Azure Arc** (Azure extension for SQL Server on Arc-enabled servers) for a move to **pay-as-you-go (PAYG)**. It only reads Azure Resource Graph and changes nothing. Scope is Azure Arc only; Azure VMs are outside `-Target Arc`.\n\n> Informational only. It does not prove Software Assurance entitlement, billing, CSP consent or compliance. Confirm charges in Cost Management and entitlement through the customer licensing process. Core numbers are estimates, not meters.\n\n## Guided path (8 steps)\nFollow the steps in order. Each step says where to look, what to do and when you can move on. Use the buttons below the text to jump to the tab.\n\n**Step 1 · Set the scope.** In the *Subscription* parameter select the subscriptions to review. The workbook only sees what your account can read in Azure Resource Graph. *Done when* the list matches the subscriptions you own for SQL.\n\n**Step 2 · Read the baseline (Summary tab).** Read the tiles top to bottom: *Hosts with SQL instances*, then *Hosts with Arc machine in ARG*; the difference is the instances whose Arc machine is not in ARG (possibly stale). Then *Arc not connected*, the license mix (*Paid*, *PAYG*, *LicenseOnly*, *LicenseType not set*) and *High priority hosts*. *Done when* you have noted these numbers as the baseline.\n\n**Step 3 · Fix the base first (Inventory and Validation tabs).** Problems here make every later number unreliable.\n- Inventory: filter rows with the flag *No Arc machine* or *Arc: Disconnected/Expired*. Reconnect the agent, or remove the stale instance resource (customer action outside this workbook).\n- Validation: the tables *SQL discovered, extension missing* (install the extension) and *Arc not connected with SQL extension* (restore Arc; the review tab flags a PAYG host that stays offline beyond 30 days).\n*Done when* the 🔴 hosts caused by these reasons are fixed or explained.\n\n**Step 4 · Triage hosts (PAYG review tab).** Start with 🔴, then 🟠. For each host read *ScriptSelection*, *ConversionRisk* and *NextAction*. Write down the hosts to **exclude** from conversion: LicenseOnly, Server+CAL, pCore applied, passive HA/DR, free/test editions. *Done when* every 🔴 and 🟠 host has a decision.\n\n**Step 5 · Check cores (Architecture tab).** Confirm VM versus physical and the core estimate of the hosts you plan to convert; consider pCore with unlimited virtualization where it applies. Core values are estimates, not billing: confirm them with the licensing owner. *Done when* the core list is agreed.\n\n**Step 6 · Check prerequisites (Validation tab).** tables *SQL 2014/2016 and ESU*, *Recurring PAYG consent and CSP*, *Auto-deploy tags*, *SQLServerLicense resources* and *Hosts with pCore applied*. *Done when* every host you will convert has no open item.\n\n**Step 7 · Dry run with the official script.** Run [manage-payg-transition.ps1](https://github.com/microsoft/sql-server-samples/blob/e1163bff690ef8b3109d83dd139ffdf1a40219da/samples/manage/manage-payg-transition/manage-payg-transition.ps1) with `-ReportOnly` and compare its list with the tile *Script would select (ARG)* and the table *Script ARG discovery filters* (PAYG review tab). Investigate every difference. *Done when* the lists match or the gap is explained.\n\n**Step 8 · Pilot and confirm.** Convert a small approved set with `-WaitForCompletion` ([Learn: PAYG transition](https://learn.microsoft.com/sql/sql-server/azure-arc/manage-pay-as-you-go-transition)). Confirm charges in [Cost Management](https://portal.azure.com/#view/Microsoft_Azure_CostManagement/Menu/~/costanalysis) and set the auto-deploy tag ([Learn: auto-deploy](https://learn.microsoft.com/sql/sql-server/azure-arc/manage-autodeploy)). Re-open this workbook: *Already PAYG* should grow, and the Validation tab section *PAYG change history* shows what changed and when (recent changes only; keep the CSV snapshots for older evidence) and the pilot hosts leave the review lists. *Done when* the pilot is confirmed; then repeat for the next wave.\n\n*Optional:* the *SQL on Azure VMs* tab covers SQL Server on Azure VMs, which are outside the Arc script.\n\n## Tabs\n| Tab | Use it for |\n|---|---|\n| **Summary** | Tiles, license mix, versions and support status |\n| **PAYG review** | Per-host priority, what the script would convert, next action; reconciliation backlog |\n| **Inventory** | Full exportable evidence |\n| **Architecture / cores** | VM vs physical signal, core estimate, pCore and unlimited virtualization options |\n| **Validations** | Auto-deploy tags, missing extension, ESU, CSP consent, connectivity, SQLServerLicense and pCore alignment |\n| **SQL on Azure VMs** | SQL Server on Azure VMs (Microsoft.SqlVirtualMachine): license type and paid editions, outside the Arc script |\n| **References** | Official links and execution flow |\n\n## Priority\n🔴 **High**: no Arc machine in ARG, Arc not connected, extension missing or not Succeeded, or the script would convert LicenseOnly, Server+CAL or pCore hosts. 🟠 **Medium**: HADR, free/test, license type not set, SQL discovery not true, SQL 2014/2016 without ESU, other-cloud VM. 🟢 **OK**: no blocker found by metadata.\n\n## Core estimate (not billing)\nUsage is metered per operating system environment, minimum 4 cores; the Standard compute-capacity approximation is 24 through 2022 and 32 for 2025, not a billing cap; Developer, Evaluation and Express are not billed; passive HA/DR candidates count 0 on Windows, but on Linux all instances are billed as active. VM uses vCPU, bare metal uses physical cores. Hosts with pCore applied may be covered by a physical core license.\n\n## What the script really does (source commit e1163bf and Microsoft Learn)\n- Selects every machine with SQL discovered, a Microsoft.AzureData extension in Succeeded and `LicenseType != PAYG`. That includes **Paid, LicenseOnly, Server+CAL and unset** hosts.\n- `-UsePcoreLicense` defaults to **No**: hosts with pCore applied are unset.\n- The wrapper does **not** pass recurring consent or exclusion tags. For CSP subscriptions use the Azure Policy \"Arc-enabled SQL Server license type compliance\" or `modify-license-type.ps1 -LicenseType PAYG -ConsentToRecurringPAYG Yes`.\n- Without `-targetSubscription` the scope is every accessible subscription in the tenant. Pass `-TenantId`.\n- Without `-WaitForCompletion` a result of `RequestSubmitted` means accepted, not applied.\n- README: Disconnected or Expired agents cannot be updated. The README also mentions tagging subscriptions with `ArcSQLServerExtensionDeployment:PAYG`; the code in the analyzed commit does not apply it, so set the tag yourself.\n\n## Glossary\n**PAYG** hourly pay-as-you-go. **Paid** attests SA or SQL subscription. **LicenseOnly** perpetual, free, SPLA or Server+CAL. **pCore** physical core license with unlimited virtualization (Enterprise). **OSE** operating system environment. **ESU** Extended Security Updates. **ReportOnly** script dry run.\n"
            },
