    {
      "type": 12,
      "content": {
        "version": "NotebookGroup/1.0",
        "groupType": "editable",
        "items": [
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "## Recommended execution path\n1. Review this workbook, 🔴 first.\n2. Run `manage-payg-transition.ps1 -Target Arc -TenantId <tenant-id> -targetSubscription <subscription-id> [-targetResourceGroup <rg>] -TargetLicenseType PAYG -ReportOnly`. Choose `-UsePcoreLicense Yes` only with a verified, active physical core license; the default `No` unsets pCore.\n3. Reconcile the newest `ModifiedResources_*.csv` (UpdateResult, UpdateError) with the Script discovery tile. Remove LicenseOnly, Server+CAL and pCore hosts from scope. No matches means no CSV.\n4. For CSP subscriptions register consent first (Azure Policy or `modify-license-type.ps1`).\n5. Pilot with `-WaitForCompletion`; validate `LicenseType = PAYG`, pCore, extension state and **Cost Management**. Rerun `-ReportOnly`: a converged scope reports nothing.\n6. Set the `ArcSQLServerExtensionDeployment` tag and monitor connectivity (30 days).\n\n## References\n- Manage licensing and billing: https://learn.microsoft.com/sql/sql-server/azure-arc/manage-license-billing\n- Transition at scale (script, dry run, Azure Policy): https://learn.microsoft.com/sql/sql-server/manage-license-type-at-scale\n- Move to pay-as-you-go, consent and connectivity: https://learn.microsoft.com/sql/sql-server/azure-arc/manage-pay-as-you-go-transition\n- Automatic connection and tags: https://learn.microsoft.com/sql/sql-server/azure-arc/manage-autodeploy\n- Configure SQL Server enabled by Azure Arc: https://learn.microsoft.com/sql/sql-server/azure-arc/manage-configuration\n- Extended Security Updates: https://learn.microsoft.com/sql/sql-server/azure-arc/extended-security-updates\n- Script (commit e1163bff690ef8b3109d83dd139ffdf1a40219da): https://github.com/microsoft/sql-server-samples/blob/e1163bff690ef8b3109d83dd139ffdf1a40219da/samples/manage/manage-payg-transition/manage-payg-transition.ps1\n- Script README: https://github.com/microsoft/sql-server-samples/blob/master/samples/manage/manage-payg-transition/README.md\n- Resource Graph query language limits: https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/governance/resource-graph/concepts/query-language\n- Workbook result limits: https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-monitor/visualize/workbooks-limits\n"
            },
            "name": "execution_refs",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "Language",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "EN"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "## Roteiro de execução recomendado\n1. Revise este workbook, começando pelos 🔴.\n2. Execute `manage-payg-transition.ps1 -Target Arc -TenantId <tenant-id> -targetSubscription <subscription-id> [-targetResourceGroup <rg>] -TargetLicenseType PAYG -ReportOnly`. Use `-UsePcoreLicense Yes` só com licença de núcleos físicos ativa e validada; o padrão `No` desativa pCore.\n3. Reconcilie o `ModifiedResources_*.csv` mais recente (UpdateResult, UpdateError) com o bloco de filtros do script. Retire do escopo hosts LicenseOnly, Server+CAL e pCore. Sem correspondências, não há CSV.\n4. Em assinaturas CSP, registre o consentimento antes (Azure Policy ou `modify-license-type.ps1`).\n5. Pilote com `-WaitForCompletion`; valide `LicenseType = PAYG`, pCore, estado da extensão e o **Cost Management**. Rode `-ReportOnly` de novo: escopo convergido não retorna nada.\n6. Defina a tag `ArcSQLServerExtensionDeployment` e monitore a conectividade (30 dias).\n\n## Referências\n- Licenciamento e cobrança: https://learn.microsoft.com/sql/sql-server/azure-arc/manage-license-billing\n- Transição em escala (script, simulação, Azure Policy): https://learn.microsoft.com/sql/sql-server/manage-license-type-at-scale\n- Migração para pay-as-you-go, consentimento e conectividade: https://learn.microsoft.com/sql/sql-server/azure-arc/manage-pay-as-you-go-transition\n- Conexão automática e tags: https://learn.microsoft.com/sql/sql-server/azure-arc/manage-autodeploy\n- Configuração do SQL habilitado por Arc: https://learn.microsoft.com/sql/sql-server/azure-arc/manage-configuration\n- Extended Security Updates: https://learn.microsoft.com/sql/sql-server/azure-arc/extended-security-updates\n- Script (commit e1163bff690ef8b3109d83dd139ffdf1a40219da): https://github.com/microsoft/sql-server-samples/blob/e1163bff690ef8b3109d83dd139ffdf1a40219da/samples/manage/manage-payg-transition/manage-payg-transition.ps1\n- README do script: https://github.com/microsoft/sql-server-samples/blob/master/samples/manage/manage-payg-transition/README.md\n- Limites da linguagem do Resource Graph: https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/governance/resource-graph/concepts/query-language\n- Limites de resultados de Workbooks: https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-monitor/visualize/workbooks-limits\n"
            },
